    <DataNode elementId="NARINGENIN-CMPD" textLabel="(2S)-naringenin" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="FTVWIRXFELQLPI-ZDUSSCGKSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="600" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment>|FRAME: NARINGENIN-CMPD| is a flavanone that is abundant in citrus fruit, where it mainly occurs as glycosides such as |FRAME: NARINGENIN-7-O-BETA-D-GLUCOSIDE| (naringenin-7-glucoside), |FRAME: NARINGIN| (the predominant flavanone in grapefruit), or |FRAME: CPD-7059|. It is also present in tomato. The naringenin and its glycosides content undergoes significant changes upon phytopathogen attack, and thus it appears that these compounds participate in the defense mechanism of |FRAME:TAX-2706| species and may act as fungicides |CITS: [15053528]|. |FRAME: NARINGIN Naringin| has been investigated with respect to its ability to scavenge oxygen free radicals involved in the oxidation of hemoglobin |CITS: [12967034]|, lowering the plasma total cholesterol level |CITS: [14738906]| and blocking the cytotoxity and apoptosis of |FRAME: CPD-15099| (Ara-C), a chemotherapeutical drug used for acute leukemia |CITS: [15135655]|. The bitterness of certain citrus species such as grapefruit (|FRAME:TAX-37656|), bitter orange (|FRAME:TAX-43166|) and pummelo (|FRAME:TAX-37334|) is caused by flavanone neohesperidosides such as naringin, in which a rhamnose is attached via the C-2 hydroxyl group of glucose. Flavanone rutinosides such as |FRAME: CPD-7059|, in which the L-rhamnose attached to the C-6 hydroxyl group of the glucose moiety, are tasteless and occur predominantly in sweet citrus fruits such as orange (|FRAME:TAX-2711|) and mandarin (&lt;i&gt;Citrus reticulata&lt;/i&gt;) |CITS: [15361143]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="NARINGENIN-CMPD" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Zinc" value="ZINC000000156701" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Metanetx" value="MNXM556" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Refmet" value="Naringenin" />
